  "notes": "\"More diatonic than trap's norm\" is the line that decides this file, and it is authored as the highest `chordToneBias` in the batch (0.85) against the lowest `halfStepDissonance` bar one, with major-key families sitting alongside the minor ones and major key spellings added to the parent's minor-only set. The second decision is the kit: the research calls it a low-aggression kit that sits under a melodic sample, so `velocityTiers` is authored down across all three tiers — accents that stop at 112 rather than 127 — which is a parameter no other entry in this batch touches, and it is the honest way to make a kit quieter without making it sparser. The sample-flip palette is `chopped_vocal`; the hook's narrow catchy contour is a step share of 0.72 with `octaveJumpProb` at 0.06. ⚠ `medium` per the research's own rating: construction is clear from the records but workflow sourcing is thin. ⚠ The filter-sweep transitions the research names are not authored — there is no filter parameter in the model, and inventing one would be dead. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
